\title{A stream of matches can be folded}
\taxon{Change}
\date{2026-11-17}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{schrodingerzy}
\tag{changelog}
\tag{stdlib}
\tag{unreleased}
\meta{release}{Unreleased}
\meta{pr}{1066}
\import{base-macros}

\p{\code{\verb~|Matches::fold(initial, step)~} is new: it folds over the matches left in a stream, one after another, and gives the value with the place where it ended, which is the end of the text, a byte no rule matches, or a match of no bytes. \code{\verb~|Automaton::fold~} is now the fold of the stream of its matches and gives what it gave before. The fold passes its step along to itself, so a closure written at the call is compiled into the loop: such a fold runs about half the instructions it ran as a loop over \code{\verb~|scan~}. See [the session](ses-A1OD).}

\p{In review as \pr{1066}.}
